@startuml
skinparam lifelineStrategy solid
autonumber
title Diagrama Devoluciones 4: POST /api/v1/refunds/:id/levels/current/view (Sellar la primera apertura del nivel)

actor "Aprobador del nivel" as Approver
participant "App Web" as Web
participant "Gateway Controller" as Gateway
participant "Refund Workflow Service" as Service
participant "Transaction Manager\n(QueryRunner)" as TX
participant "refund_workflow_instance_levels DB" as LevelsDB
participant "refund_workflow_actions DB" as ActionsDB

Approver -> Web: Abre el detalle de la nota estando en su bandeja
Web -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/refunds/2001/levels/current/view
note right of Web
  El FE lo llama una sola vez al montar
  el detalle, y solo si el usuario es
  aprobador del nivel activo.
end note
Gateway -> Service: registerLevelFirstView(refundOrderId: 2001, actor)

Service -> LevelsDB: 1. findCurrentLevel(instanceId)
LevelsDB --> Service: level { id: 201, status: 'IN_PROGRESS',\nfirst_viewed_at: NULL }

Service -> Service: 2. assertViewerIsApprover(level, actor)
note right of Service
  403 si el actor no pertenece al rol del nivel.
  Que un tercero mire el detalle NO sella nada.
end note

alt first_viewed_at IS NULL
    Service -> TX: 3. startTransaction()
    activate TX

    Service -> LevelsDB: 4. sealFirstView(201, actor.employeeCode, NOW())
    note right of LevelsDB
      - first_viewed_at = NOW()
      - first_viewed_by = actor
      Se sella una sola vez: las aperturas
      siguientes no lo mueven.
    end note
    LevelsDB --> Service: ok

    Service -> ActionsDB: 5. insertWorkflowAction(instanceId, 201, 'VIEWED')
    ActionsDB --> Service: ok

    Service -> TX: 6. commitTransaction()
    deactivate TX
else Ya estaba sellado
    Service -> Service: 7. skipWrite()
    note right of Service
      Idempotente: responde 200 sin escribir.
    end note
end

Service --> Gateway: 200 OK (LevelViewResult: { firstViewedAt, firstViewedBy })
Gateway --> Web: 200 OK
Web --> Approver: Renderiza el detalle con el plazo (SLA) corriendo
@enduml
